## Description
This PR contains a port from the harvest script to the new "Scripts and Processes" system in DSpace 7. 

Furthermore, the REST -h option has been improved to show more information about the different arguments instead of just a list of arguments. 

## Instructions for Reviewers
Verify that the harvest script can still be used as before from both the CLI and the REST: 
1. Use the -h option from both the CLI and REST and verify that they contain similar information about how to use the script.
2. Use the -s option as specified in the help option to setup a collection for harvesting. 
```
POST {{url}}/api/system/scripts/harvest/processes
properties: 
[
  {
    "name": "-s"
  },
  {
    "name": "-c",
    "value": "{{collection-handle}}"
  },
  {
    "name": "-a",
    "value": "{{oai-server-address}}"
  },
  {
    "name": "-i",
    "value": "com_2384_294335"
  },
  {
    "name": "-m",
    "value": "dc"
} ,
  {
    "name": "-t",
    "value": "1"
  }
]
```
3. Use the -r option as specified in the help option to run the harvest on the previously configured collection. 
```
POST  {{url}}/api/system/scripts/harvest/processes
properties: 
[
  {
    "name": "-r"
  },
  {
    "name": "-c",
    "value": "{{collection-handle}}"
  },
  {
    "name": "-e",
    "value": "{{user-email}}"
  }
]
```
4. Verify that items are harvested in the collection and that "api/core/collections/{collection-uuid}/harvester" contains the harvest config you set up in step 2 and the harvest start time from step 3. 
5. Use the -p option as specified in the help option to purge the collection from the harvested items.
```
POST  {{url}}/api/system/scripts/harvest/processes
properties: 
[
  {
    "name": "-p"
  },
  {
    "name": "-c",
    "value": "{{collection-handle}}"
  },
  {
    "name": "-e",
    "value": "{{user-email}}"
  }
]
```

